Note struct: id, title, body, tags, pinned. The text format is: id \n---\n title \
n---\n pinned("1"/"0") \n---\n body.

Split on "\n---\n" and require exactly 4 parts. pinned: "1" → true, "0" → false. Should
 anything other than "1"/"0" throw malformedFormat? The spec says the pinned flag
 is "1" or "0", and it says to throw when the split doesn't yield exactly 4 parts
. For pinned values other than "1"/"0", it's safest to throw malformedFormat ("rather
 than guessing"). Parse pinned: "1" → true, "0" → false, otherwise throw.

Implement with patch.
